Text: "Logic distinguishes the form of an argument from the subject matter of
       its sentences. The chapter begins with truth-functional connectives,
       passes to predicates and quantifiers, and ends with the notions of
       semantic consequence, derivation, proof, and mathematical definition.
       This order matters: connectives combine assertions, quantifiers bind
       variables inside assertions, and proofs certify that conclusions follow
       from stated assumptions."
Id: "7fef7b05-b210-4e85-87e3-1bcdf99aa3f8"
